WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.850
- Hey, guys. Welcome to another episode

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:03.160
of the Wednesday checkup.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.620
It feels like we haven't done
one of those intros in awhile.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.610
But that's because we've been busy

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.410
talking about the novel coronavirus.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.690
Today, we're gonna be looking at some

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.230
of the most common conspiracy theories

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.986
I've seen and heard out there.

00:00:13.986 --> 00:00:16.060
Shane Dawson, I'm looking at you.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.360
We're doing the medical version.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.802
Medical conspiracy time.

00:00:18.802 --> 00:00:21.385
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.100
The government introduced
the coronavirus in 2018

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.840
and Bill Gates was somehow responsible.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.350
Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation is one

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.920
of the most humanitarian foundations

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.160
in the world, financially speaking.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.660
They're literally doing
everything they can

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.306
to eradicate disease, bring
fresh water to people,

00:00:43.306 --> 00:00:45.360
and we're gonna blame this on them?

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.040
Japanese doctors treating COVID-19 cases

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.870
say that you should ensure your
mouth and throat are moist,

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:53.310
never dry, so make sure
you're taking a few sips

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.230
of water every 15 minutes.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.230
Skeptical to the source.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.720
I don't know if necessarily
Japanese doctors came out

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.650
and said this, but there's
partial truth to it.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.750
If you have dry mucous membranes,

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.520
they are more likely to crack.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.270
When they crack, you actually
have a higher possibility

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.420
of getting infected with
a bacteria or virus.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.380
So, yeah, you should be
staying well-hydrated.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.370
You should be drinking.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.360
Will it protect you a hundred percent? No.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.002
But it's a good way to make sure that

00:01:18.002 --> 00:01:20.420
you're doing the best
you can to stay healthy.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.900
Hand dryers are effective
at killing coronavirus.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.440
I don't think that's the case.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.990
It certainly hasn't been proven.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.480
Also CDC recommends drying your hands

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.040
through the air dry method,

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.260
which is you just naturally
let your hands dry,

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:34.900
or using a paper towel.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.560
Reason being ... There was a study

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.081
that I actually talked
about on this channel

00:01:38.081 --> 00:01:40.352
that showed those ultra high speed dryers

00:01:40.352 --> 00:01:43.510
actually blow bacteria and
viruses all over the place.

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.120
Especially if you don't
wash your hands well.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.580
With this virus having fecal-oral spread,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.120
meaning that toilets,
sinks, can be quite messy,

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.620
especially in public restrooms,

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.370
you don't wanna be blowing that bacteria

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.800
and viruses all over the place.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.660
So, no, I don't think air
dryers will kill the virus,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:58.990
and I don't think you
should be using them.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:03.318
You can create your own hand
sanitizer using Tito's vodka.

00:02:03.318 --> 00:02:06.170
I was almost gonna say like
yeah, it's possible to create

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.120
your own ... Not with vodka!

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.640
Not with Tito's vodka!

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.620
I actually think Tito's vodka came out

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.770
and had to make a statement on this

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.640
because people were doing
this based off a TikTok video.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.010
No, you cannot use Tito's vodka,

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.310
which I think is only 40 percent alcohol

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.210
to create a hand sanitizer like that.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.360
It's just not recommended.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.820
If you're gonna be using
some kind of disinfectant,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:30.090
the recommendation would
be to use rubbing alcohol.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.170
That being said, soap and water,

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.340
soap and water, soap and water.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.550
Gargling with salt water or vinegar

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.480
will eliminate the COVID-19 coronavirus.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.800
We have no evidence of that.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.900
I actually do recommend salt water gargles

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.444
to a lot of my patients.

00:02:44.444 --> 00:02:46.980
Not for eliminating viruses.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.999
Just because it soothes a sore throat.

00:02:48.999 --> 00:02:52.410
If you have mucous build up,
it helps clear the mucous,

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.310
especially if you have
like post nasal drip

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.220
or really chronic sore throat.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.300
But to kill the virus?

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.760
We don't have evidence of that.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.197
Also this virus seems
to be very infectious

00:03:02.197 --> 00:03:05.184
in comparison to the
influenza virus for example,

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.380
so if it touches your mucous membranes,

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.830
right away it's gonna start
infecting the rest of your body.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.277
It has a long incubation period,

00:03:12.277 --> 00:03:14.160
but a quick infection period,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.140
if that makes any sense.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.670
Coronavirus originated with Chinese people

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.110
eating bats from open air markets.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:24.020
Okay, I heard this one, and
initially I was almost ready

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.690
to buy into that, because, you know,

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.840
other cultures eat different animals,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.300
so I wasn't one to judge.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.900
However, when I looked in to this,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.078
I found that the initial picture
that started this reporting

00:03:34.078 --> 00:03:36.610
actually didn't come from China.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:39.120
It came from a reporter that was eating

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.850
in an asian country, not China,
some kind of local delicacy.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:44.590
Nothing to do with the cuisine

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.660
that's actually consumed in China.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.970
So, no, we have no evidence
of this coming from bat soup.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.150
We need to stop that.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:55.480
We initially thought that
this virus started in bats,

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.330
somehow made its way to humans,

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.200
probably through a mutation.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.058
There could have been an
intermediate carrier along the way,

00:04:02.058 --> 00:04:05.089
so perhaps a bat passed
it to another animal,

00:04:05.089 --> 00:04:06.840
and then we got into humans.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:07.840
We don't know that yet.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:09.190
We're gonna be investigating.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.210
And again, let's think smart here.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.802
We're trying to combat
this, prevent spread,

00:04:13.802 --> 00:04:16.299
flatten the curve ... I
mentioned that in my other video,

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:18.449
which basically decreases the strain

00:04:18.449 --> 00:04:20.530
that's put on our healthcare systems.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.280
What's the use in talking about bat soup

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.030
outside of getting clicks? Zero.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.710
The most dangerous or
at-risk place you can go

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.270
is a train or subway.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.000
The most dangerous place
you could probably go

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.470
is a hospital or an emergency room

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.660
with people sneezing and
coughing all over the place.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.330
That is why we have
been directing patients

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.760
to call in ahead of time to figure out

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.190
if their symptoms are mild enough

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.930
so we can get them to stay home

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:47.510
so they don't spread their virus

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.110
and they don't catch anyone else's.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.070
One of the biggest problems
we face in the hospital

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.080
is known as nosocomial infection.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:54.020
I know that's a mouthful.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.390
Basically means that you got sick

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.740
from being in the hospital.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.360
If you notice, doctors are always trying

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.390
to get all the tests done,
give you all your treatments,

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.400
so that we can send you
home from the hospital.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.500
It's not because we don't
enjoy having you there.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.720
It's because we don't want
you to catch a disease

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.300
accidentally in the hospital.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.490
It happens. There's
sick people all around.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.160
Some people don't wash their hands well.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.170
They sneeze in the hallway.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.120
You walk through it.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.440
There's all sorts of issues.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:19.290
So while I do think being in
a crowded subway is not good,

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.570
being in a place where
there's a lot of sick people

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.970
is probably a tad worse.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.690
That's why you should be going
only in cases of emergency

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.300
or when you need serious
medical advice or help.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.482
That's why most routine
procedures, surgeries,

00:05:31.482 --> 00:05:34.960
well checks, all have been pushed aside

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.960
in order to prevent
patients from coming in

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.480
and catching COVID-19.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.750
The Simpsons predicted the coronavirus.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.330
The Simpsons, the novels, no.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.070
No one could have predicted this.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.240
Yes, we knew that there was a possibility

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.790
of another pandemic happening.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.830
It happens. With each
generation I think it happens.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:54.790
The last one that, to me,
rings the biggest bell

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.270
is the Spanish Flu of 1918.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.250
That claimed millions of lives.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.990
Hopefully now with modern medicine,

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.020
our ability to communicate, our ability

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.960
to create technology like vaccines

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.560
and antiviral medications rather quickly,

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:09.000
hopefully we're gonna do a better job.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.540
An Irish company is preparing

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.210
to release rapid COVID-19 testing kits,

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.830
which could provide results in 15 minutes.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.050
That would be awesome, because
we need more testing kits.

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:20.193
If we could get them done
quickly, very important.

00:06:20.193 --> 00:06:23.400
However, these tests,
especially the rapid ones

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.390
need to be heavily scrutinized
through clinical trials

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.830
because we need to
establish the sensitivity

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.260
and the specificity of those tests.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:32.640
Both of those need to be high.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.840
I'll explain each of them.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.580
A test that has high sensitivity

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.470
is good for screening,
meaning taking general people

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.120
in the population and trying to find out

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.700
if they have a specific disease.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.170
In a highly sensitive test,
you have few false negatives.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.430
On a highly specific test,
you have few false positives.

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.780
The ideal way of doing
this is you give someone

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.330
as a screening test, a
highly sensitive one,

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:55.819
and then you can give them
a highly specific test

00:06:55.819 --> 00:06:58.020
to confirm that diagnosis.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.090
Now, in a test like this,
where you're testing people

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.660
who are already sick, it's
not necessarily screening.

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:06.130
It's more diagnostic, and a
good diagnostic test has both.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.090
High sensitivity and specificity.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:10.260
There are many supplements and other cures

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.360
that can fight off the coronavirus.

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:15.450
We have zero evidence for
any of those statements,

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.140
and I'm so proud of
the FDA for prosecuting

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.994
those individuals trying
to make claims like this.

00:07:19.994 --> 00:07:22.979
John Oliver had a segment
of someone trying to sell

00:07:22.979 --> 00:07:25.963
silver as a way to get rid of the virus.

00:07:26.933 --> 00:07:31.090
No. No! And if you're a
supplement manufacturer,

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.340
or you have your own line of supplements,

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:37.150
please do not use this as a
moment to brand your product.

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:40.790
That is a cheap shot, praying
at folks' vulnerabilities

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.710
at a very sensitive time.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:45.270
We should be banding together,
not trying to figure out

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:46.840
how to make a buck off each other.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:49.590
Four women in Wuhan have
given birth to babies

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:52.580
who do not have the coronavirus,
unlike their mothers.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.180
There's been some evidence showing that

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.720
what we call vertical transmission,

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:00.150
from the mother to the
baby inside the uterus,

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.780
there isn't transmission.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.660
That's not to say it can't happen,

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.810
but the evidence for
it does look promising.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:07.200
We're hoping it stays that way.

